  "narrative": {
    "status": "retried",
    "headline": "Power Backup Report for Harris County",
    "summary": "Homes in Harris County face a long outage about once every 5 years based on 8 years of records since 2018. In one big storm 91% of homes in the county lost power. The longest-waiting tenth waited about 175 hours. Another storm hit 28% of homes in the county with the longest-waiting tenth out about 140 hours. One Core lasts about 15 hours in August. One Core lasts about 42 hours in January. Two Cores last about 25 hours in August. Two Cores cover 46% of past 12-hour-plus outage hours. Base confirms sizing at install.",
